Small naming cleanup — not urgent.

⸻

🔶 4️⃣ “Soft Gate” vs “Hard Gate” Language Inconsistency

Stage 3.5 is called Soft Gate but halts if escalation remains Open.

Stage 4.5 is Soft Gate but can HALT.

They are actually:

Conditionally Hard Gates.

You may want to standardize terminology:
	•	Hard Gate → always halts on failure
	•	Conditional Gate → may pass/warn/halt based on mode
	•	Integrity Gate → always halts

Right now the semantics require interpretation.

⸻

🔶 5️⃣ You Have Not Defined Concurrency Behavior

What if:

Two cycles for two releases run concurrently?

State is local per cycle folder — good.

But backlog update step modifies shared file.

You may eventually need:
	•	“Active release lock” rule
	•	Or “only one cycle may update backlog at a time”

Not urgent — but important if scaled.

